                <pb facs="0742" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/2272: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Barcelona</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Franklin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-26T12:00:00-04:00">July 26, 1936—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 25, 7 p.m. This message has been transmitted to the Commander of the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Quincy</hi> with instructions to investigate the
                    situation. In view of the fact that the Commander of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Quincy</hi> will be in constant contact with Washington, and points along
                    the Spanish coast, it is felt that the movement of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Quincy</hi> should be left to the discretion of its Commander.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
